course: dictionary
lesson: 7842
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket or bat.» Here a racket is something you swing, so it must be the sports kind.
explain: Racket can also mean a loud, unpleasant noise. A parent might say, «Stop that racket!» when children are shouting. The words around it tell you the meaning: someone is making a noise, not holding a bat.
explain: A third meaning is a dishonest way of getting money. This meaning often shows up in safety lessons. Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always check which one fits.
fact: «Racket» means a bat with a frame and strings, used to hit the ball in tennis, badminton or squash.
fact: «Racket» can also mean a loud, unpleasant noise, as in «What a racket!»
fact: «Racket» can also mean a dishonest way of getting money, a trick or a scam.
exercise: «Keep a safe distance from anyone swinging a racket or bat.» What is a racket in this sentence? | A dishonest trick | A small ball | A loud, unpleasant noise | *A bat with a frame and strings
exercise: Dad shouts, «Stop that racket!» What does racket mean here? | A dishonest way of getting money | *A loud, unpleasant noise | A quiet game | A tennis bat
exercise: Which meaning of racket fits «The man tricked old people out of their savings. It was a racket»? | A happy party | *A dishonest way of getting money | A sports bat | A loud, unpleasant noise
test: Mason smashed his racket after losing and yelled, «Bro, that line judge is sus!» What does racket mean here? | A scam | A bag for sports kit | A loud noise | *A tennis bat
test: Ella says a racket is a loud noise, but her sister says it is a scam. How can you find out which meaning is right? | Choose the first meaning you see in the dictionary | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Ask someone who is not in the room | Guess the one that sounds nicest
exam: «The children made such a racket that the neighbours came round.» Which meaning of racket fits best? | A tennis bat | A dishonest trick | A sports match | *A loud, unpleasant noise
